#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0295-A expect=violation domain=PP
#note "The half this R-5.25 split sibling owns: row 2 populates --ENINT with an empty --STINT -> fires. Row 1 (--STINT without --ENINT) is the PARENT CDISC-SEND-0295's state and must NOT fire here - the discriminator of the split, on the same dataset the parent's violation fixture uses."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=2 USUBJID=002
dataset PP class=FINDINGS label="Pharmacokinetic Parameters"
col STUDYID  type=Char
col DOMAIN   type=Char
col USUBJID  type=Char
col PPSEQ    type=Num
col PPTESTCD type=Char
col PPSTINT  type=Char
col PPENINT  type=Char
---
S1 | PP | 001 | 1 | AUCALL | P0H  |
S1 | PP | 002 | 1 | AUCALL |      | P24H
S1 | PP | 003 | 1 | AUCALL | P0H  | P24H
S1 | PP | 004 | 1 | CMAX   |      |
